<div class="legacy-4555334f95"><strong><em><span class="legacy-303f3ed109">Pine Tree Rifle
Club&nbsp;Board of Directors&nbsp;with the clubs newest Lifetime Member GARY
STOLLER (center in back row with white shirt.</span></em></strong></div>
<div><strong><em><span class="legacy-303f3ed109"></span></em></strong>&nbsp;</div>
<div><strong><em><span class="legacy-303f3ed109">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; At
the&nbsp;November 11th, 2009 (Veteran's Day) monthly Members meeting of the Pine
Tree Rifle Club a&nbsp;motion was&nbsp;made at the meeting by the Club President
Paul Catucci that Gary Stoller be bestowed with the honor of Pine Tree Rifle
Club Lifetime Membership and and it was passed by the member unanimously. How
fitting as Gary is a veteran who was drafted into the Army back in 1966, and did
a tour of duty in Vietnam. Earning a rank of E5 and two purple hearts he was
honorably discharged in 1968.</span></em></strong></div>
<div><strong><em><span class="legacy-303f3ed109"></span></em></strong>&nbsp;</div>
<div><strong><em><span class="legacy-303f3ed109">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
Gary&nbsp;joined&nbsp;the Pine Tree Rifle Club&nbsp;in 1969 and has held many
positions in the club where he has strived to make our club the place it is
today. He also served 13 years on the clubs Board of Directors. I'm sure that
you have seen him at club fundraising events and in way too many work parties to
count. His effort and dedication to the club over the years has been
outstanding.</span></em></strong></div>
<div><strong><em><span class="legacy-303f3ed109"></span></em></strong>&nbsp;</div>
<div><strong><em><span class="legacy-303f3ed109">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; It should also be
noted that he has been a active member of the Meco Volunteer Fire Company for 44
years. Serving his country, community, and the Pine Tree Rifle Club throughout
his adult life he is an American hero. We are fortunate and proud to have him as
a club member. </span></em></strong></div>
<div><strong><em><span class="legacy-303f3ed109"></span></em></strong>&nbsp;</div>
<div><strong><em><span class="legacy-303f3ed109">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; We fellow club
members&nbsp;of the Pine Tree Rifle Club tip our hats to Gary and say THANK YOU
for all you have done for&nbsp;our club, community, and Country.
</span></em></strong></div>
